{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1387173-do-laham-stink-of-the-wyrm","id":1387173,"title":"Do Laham stink of the Wyrm?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-09T21:30:03-07:00","id":1387173,"title":"Do Laham stink of the Wyrm?","content":"Laham come from Mage. They are humans with the blood of literal demons of the High Umbra. I read that Spectres (Low Umbra) are not Wyrm tainted, so it seems likely that the High Umbra nasties likewise won\u2019t trigger any Wyrm senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T21:37:29-07:00","id":1387175,"title":"","content":"Depends on their level of entropic resonance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T22:08:19-07:00","id":1387179,"title":"","content":"Mercurial, I don't know where you read that Spectres are not Wyrm tainted, so maybe it is a new rule. But I know that previously Spectres were considered Wyrm tainted. And I've read different things concerning Wraiths. Revised Storyteller Handbook stated that if a Wraith's permanent Angst exceeds permanent Willpower that they'd detect as Wyrm as well. And I think in the Oblivion LARP rules that Sense Wyrm could detect Wraiths if they were somehow affecting the Skinlands.<br /> <br /> So I would definitely say that Laham should detect as the Wyrm unless they had some special power or reason to not.<br /> <br /> But with a lot of things in Sense Wyrm, STs can make rulings base on however they conceive of the Gift and Taint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T22:31:24-07:00","id":1387185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1387173-do-laham-stink-of-the-wyrm?p=1387179#post1387179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mercurial, I don't know where you read that Spectres are not Wyrm tainted, so maybe it is a new rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be misremembering it, but I think it was mentioned when discussing how the Dark Umbra was outside of the standard Wyld/Weaver/Wyrm paradigm and instead was it\u2019s own world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T00:15:23-07:00","id":1387200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1387173-do-laham-stink-of-the-wyrm?p=1387185#post1387185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I might be misremembering it, but I think it was mentioned when discussing how the Dark Umbra was outside of the standard Wyld/Weaver/Wyrm paradigm and instead was it\u2019s own world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh no, every realm in the umbra operates under the the powers that be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T01:05:01-07:00","id":1387204,"title":"","content":"Specters are definitely Wyrm Tainted, its normal Wraiths that aren't always.<br /> <br /> But yeah in the Tellurian all resonate with the Triat to some degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T07:52:18-07:00","id":1387270,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks. I\u2019m looking through the books now, and I can\u2019t find it. I will try and see if I simply misread a passage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T22:52:00-07:00","id":1388573,"title":"","content":"Mercurial, in CWOD, I believe Oblivion was concidered an aspect of either the Defiler Wyrm, Eater of Souls or both. Laham would definitely be Wyrm-tainted by CWOD intent, as originally written..in fact, Infernalist Nephandi were worshipping emanations of the Neverborn as demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5726-grayhoss","name":"grayhoss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}